 "traps": [
  "include(\":app:shared\") and its siblings create the intermediate project :app at app/ without any build file: it is a unit with a null manifest and a workspace member",
  "the root build.gradle.kts applies every plugin with apply false and pins Node.js 22.22.0 for the Kotlin/JS and Kotlin/Wasm plugins; it also applies gradle/releases.gradle.kts, a script that runs git",
  "every version lives in gradle/libs.versions.toml: the build files only name catalog accessors (libs.ktor.server.netty, libs.plugins.kotlinMultiplatform), and Kotlin is 2.5.0-RC, Compose Multiplatform 1.13.0-beta02, AGP 9.3.3",
  "compileSdk is release(37) with minorApiLevel 2, both read from the catalog; minSdk 28 and targetSdk 37 are not machine toolchains",
  ":app:androidApp applies com.android.application without org.jetbrains.kotlin.android: AGP 9 compiles Kotlin itself",
  ":core, :app:shared and :app:ui-components use com.android.kotlin.multiplatform.library, the KMP Android library plugin, inside kotlin { android { } }",
  "jvmToolchain(21) is in four build files, while jvmTarget is JVM_11 for Android: 21 is the JDK on the machine, 11 is only the bytecode target",
  ":app:shared adds two hand-made source sets, nonAndroidMain (for iosMain, jvmMain, webMain) and nonWebMain (for androidMain, iosMain, jvmMain); :app:ui-components adds nonAndroidMain",
  ":backend depends on :app:adminApp through a custom configuration adminPanel that pulls the jsBrowserDistribution output into the backend resources under admin/: a Kotlin/JS front end is packed inside the Ktor jar",
  "the backend main class is io.ktor.server.netty.EngineMain, a library class: the real entry points are the four modules listed in backend/src/main/resources/application.yaml",
  "the iOS app is an Xcode project, not a Gradle project: its Compile Kotlin build phase calls ./gradlew :app:shared:embedAndSignAppleFrameworkForXcode and Swift imports the framework as shared",
  "app/iosApp/KotlinMultiplatformLinkedPackage holds empty .m, .h and module.modulemap stubs and a subpackage named after the Maven coordinate io.github.mirzemehdi:kmpnotifier-push-firebase:2.0.2, which asks for firebase-ios-sdk from 12.14.0: the folder is written by a tool, not by hand; its empty Objective-C stubs carry no language",
  "the two Package.resolved files (KotlinConf.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace and KotlinConf.xcworkspace) disagree: grpc-binary 1.69.1 against 1.69.0 and gtm-session-fetcher 4.5.0 against 4.4.0; firebase-ios-sdk is 12.19.3 in both",
  "kotlin-js-store/yarn.lock and kotlin-js-store/wasm/yarn.lock are lockfiles the Kotlin Gradle plugin keeps for the npm packages of the JS and Wasm targets (npm(\"@js-joda/timezone\", \"3.2.1\") in :app:shared); there is no package.json in the repository",
  "Procfile and app.json describe a Heroku deploy of the backend jar with -Dorg.gradle.project.INCLUDE_ANDROID=false, a property no build file reads",
  "the devcontainer image is mcr.microsoft.com/devcontainers/java:1-21 and its feature installs Maven 3.8.6, although nothing in the project uses Maven",
  "backend/src/main/resources/years/ and backend/src/test/resources/years/ hold Markdown documents and JSON the API serves as content: they are data, not documentation of the project",
  "the backend reaches PostgreSQL when DB0_HOST is set and otherwise opens an H2 file database in PostgreSQL mode",
  "app/webApp/src/webMain/resources/service-worker.js is entirely commented out",
  "source_sets are given only for the JVM and Android modules, where the plugin conventions fix them; the KMP modules list their existing kotlin folders as source roots and the targets as build_tags",
  "languages lists programming and markup languages only; XML, JSON, YAML, TOML, SVG and Markdown files are present and not listed",
  "connections is a sample of 26 points: the backend routes with the shared and admin clients that call them, the admin bundle served by the backend, :core shared by three units, the iOS framework, Firebase, the database, Sessionize and the production base URL"
 ]
}
